# Build output
bin/
obj/
publish/
native/
*.user
*.suo

# Visual Studio's per-user state and index files. These are machine-specific, sometimes locked
# by a running IDE (which makes `git add` fail outright), and never belong in the history.
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Signing material must never enter the repository. The certificate and its private key live
# outside the project tree (see tools/sign.ps1) precisely so that they cannot be committed by
# accident and can be shared with other projects.
*.pfx
*.pvk
*.snk
*.cer
*.crt
*.key

# Scratch directories used while developing and verifying
_*/
rattrap-out/

# The original C++ probes under probe/ keep their sources, the probe scripts and the text logs,
# because those logs are the evidence behind docs/measured-behaviour.md. What is excluded is what
# can be rebuilt or regenerated: compiled objects, and the raw BGRA dumps (about 9.5 MB of them,
# reproducible by rerunning the probes).
probe/build/
*.bgra
*.obj
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.lib

# Transient output
*.log

_*

